# What may be uploaded to Vercel. Deny-by-default, and deliberately so.
#
# Vercel CLI does NOT read .gitignore. Its documented default-exclusion list
# contains ".gitignore" as A FILENAME TO SKIP UPLOADING, never as a source of
# rules, and its docs say plainly: "Aside from the default exclusions, all files
# within your project are uploaded to Vercel if no source path is specified to
# be excluded in a .vercelignore configuration file."
#
# Without this file, `vercel deploy` from the repository root uploads:
#   data.json        5,283,444 bytes -- this player's save, carrying 183 other
#                    players' 12-digit owner_viewer_id values. Those people
#                    never used this tool and cannot consent, which is the whole
#                    reason for the parse-and-discard decision (2026-09-15).
#   master.mdb       16,773,120 bytes of the game's own database.
#   master.mdb.old   16,580,608 bytes of the previous patch's copy.
#
# A Git-connected deployment is safe without this, because the integration only
# clones committed files. The CLI is the dangerous path, and the CLI is this
# project's release path: releases run through `vercel build` rather than a
# git push.
#
# ALLOWLIST, not a denylist. A denylist protects the files somebody remembered;
# the next sensitive file added to this repo would upload silently. Here the
# failure direction is a build error, which is loud and cheap. Add new
# top-level paths deliberately.

# Ignore everything at the repository root...
/*

# ...then re-admit exactly what a deployment needs.
!package.json
!package-lock.json
!tsconfig.base.json
!vercel.json
!packages

# `!packages` re-admits the WHOLE subtree, so re-deny inside it. Build output
# and installs are produced on Vercel, never shipped to it.
packages/*/node_modules
packages/*/*.tsbuildinfo

# Build output, both packages. The api service's entrypoint is src/main.ts, so
# nothing uploaded needs a compiled dist -- Vercel builds its own.
packages/*/dist

# The artwork under packages/web/public is committed and uploaded. See NOTICE.md.
